Q: Terminate called after throwing an instance of &#39;char const*&#39; A: <p>Based on the discussion on the OP, I recommend that you keep the file name as a <code>QString</code>. Replace <code>char* bmpName;</code> with <code>QString strBmpName;</code> in your header. Then convert the <code>QString</code> to a <code>char*</code> for the following line.</p>
<pre><code>BmpFile bm(MainWindow::bmpName);
</code></pre>
<p>to</p>
<pre><code>QByteArray ba = strBmpName.toLocal8Bit();
BmpFile bm(ba.data());
</code></pre>

Q: How do you debug a Linux core dump using VSCode? A: <p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/kG0LnTb8.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer">VIew Selection dialog</a></p>
<p>This has been tested on vscode 1.106.3<br />
It works very well, allows you to choose the dump you want and then jumps right into the debugger where the exception occurd.</p>
<p>When you run you will get a list with previous coredumps</p>
<p>I was thinking of making a vscode extension for this, will consider it when I have free time</p>
<p>Update  <code>/usr/bin/my_program</code></p>
<p>You need to install this extension  <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=augustocdias.tasks-shell-input" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Shell Input Extension</a><br />
You also need to have coredumpctl</p>
<p>My Taks.json</p>
<pre><code>{
    &quot;version&quot;: &quot;2.0.0&quot;,
    &quot;tasks&quot;: [
        {
            &quot;label&quot;: &quot;coredump&quot;,
            &quot;type&quot;: &quot;shell&quot;,
            // We use 'cut' to grab the string before the first pipe '|'
            &quot;command&quot;: &quot;PICKED='${input:selectedPidString}'; PID=$(echo \&quot;$PICKED\&quot; | awk '{print $1}'); echo \&quot;Selected PID: $PID\&quot;; coredumpctl dump $PID --output=${workspaceFolder}/build/dump.core&quot;,
            &quot;problemMatcher&quot;: []
        }
    ],
    &quot;inputs&quot;: [
        {
            &quot;id&quot;: &quot;selectedPidString&quot;,
            &quot;type&quot;: &quot;command&quot;,
            &quot;command&quot;: &quot;shellCommand.execute&quot;,
            &quot;args&quot;: {
                // Using $5 because 'EAT' is $4 and the PID follows it
//You can remove the program path to view a list of all dumps on your system
                &quot;command&quot;: &quot;coredumpctl list /usr/bin/my_program  --no-legend | tac | awk '{printf \&quot;%s | %s %s %s | %s | %s | %s\\n\&quot;, $5, $2, $3, $4, $8, $11, $10}'&quot;,
                &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Select: PID | Date Time TZ | Signal | Size | Path&quot;,
                &quot;useSingleQuote&quot;: true,
                &quot;useStandardOutput&quot;: true
            }
        }
    ]
}
</code></pre>
<p>This is the launch.json</p>
<pre><code>   {
            &quot;name&quot;: &quot;(GDB) Launch tracker with coredump&quot;,
            &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cppdbg&quot;,
